# Runtime worker protocol files written into a worktree by an external
# orchestrator. They are private operational instructions -- internal role
# names, local endpoints, dispatcher behaviour -- and belong to whoever
# generated them, not to this public repository (docs/public-private-boundary.md
# forbids exactly that content here). Ignored so a `git add -A` inside such a
# worktree cannot sweep one into a commit, which is how one reached PR #79.
.claude/
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md

# Documented fixture contracts are committed source, not runtime data.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl
